<PageLayout title="About TechSpotlight News" description="Who writes TechSpotlight News, who it's for, and why you can trust it.">
  <p>Hi, I'm <strong>{SITE.author}</strong>. I write TechSpotlight News for people like me: busy readers in India and the UAE who want to know what's changing in tech, and which apps and AI tools are actually worth their time and money.</p>

  <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
  <p>Most tech news is either too long, too technical, or written for readers in another country. I wanted something shorter and calmer. Each news brief tells you what happened, why people are talking about it, and what it means for you here, whether you're a student in Hyderabad or a professional in Dubai.</p>

  <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>News briefs:</strong> short summaries of the tech stories that matter, each with a "What this means for you" section.</li>
    <li><strong>Guides:</strong> honest, longer guides to apps and AI tools. Best-of lists, comparisons, reviews and how-tos.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How I test tools</h2>
  <p>I review software and AI tools, not hardware. I test each tool myself on its free plan or free trial before I write about it, and I tell you exactly what I tried in a "How I tested" section. If I haven't used something, I'll say so.</p>

  <h2>How this site earns money</h2>
  <p>Some links on this site are affiliate links. If you sign up or buy through one, I may earn a small commission at no extra cost to you. That never decides what I recommend. You can read the details in my <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> and <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>Say hello</h2>
  <p>Spotted a mistake, or want me to look at a tool? <a href="/contact/">Get in touch</a>. I read every message.</p>
</PageLayout>
